# KQS POS — Performance & Maintainability

## Performance targets

| Area | Rule |
|------|------|
| POS catalog API | Single warehouse query; batch item metadata; target < 2 s on store Wi-Fi |
| Layby search | Indexed fields first; `limit` capped; order by `modified desc` |
| Stock qty | Always use sellable qty (on-hand − reservations), not raw bin qty |
| Frontend | Minimize re-renders; avoid fetching full catalog on every keystroke |
| Docker dev | Do not optimize prematurely — fix measured N+1 and missing limits first |

## Growth & versioning

- **v1 scope**: layby + POS per `docs/layby-rules.md`. Flag v2 features (manager PIN, exchanges) — do not half-implement.
- New stores: configuration (Warehouse, POS Profile), not code forks.
- Website/catalog sync: reuse `api/stock.py` endpoints — one source for sellable qty.
- App version in `hooks.py` / `pyproject.toml`; document breaking API changes in `docs/`.

## Testing before merge

- Manual smoke on Docker dev: login → catalog → layby deposit → installment → complete → invoice.
- Tablet checklist in `docs/deployment.md`.
- Seed data: `kqs_retail.setup.seed_kqs_demo.seed` for reproducible dev.

## Code quality

- Python: type hints on public functions; copyright header on new files.
- No dead code, commented-out blocks, or TODO without issue reference.
- Comments only for non-obvious business rules (e.g. grace period, refund %).
- Prefer extending ERPNext DocTypes over custom parallel data models.

## Deployment

- Single till URL: `https://your-erp-site/app/point-of-sale` on store tablets.
- Backups: `bench --site all backup --with-files` (see `docs/deployment.md`).
- Staging before production for any layby or payment logic change.
